<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45845" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφυβρ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>insult over</i> one, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφυβρίζων ἕλετο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.368
				</span></i>
			: c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				1385
			</span></i>: c.acc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἀμαθίαν ὑμῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.579c
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>APl.</u>
				1.4
			</span></i> (also 
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ ᾽φυβρίζεσθαι νεκρούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1663
				</span></i>
			): with neut. Adj., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλὰ ἐ. τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Heracl.</u>
					947
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δεινὰ πόλει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					179
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ἀδελφὸν οἷ᾽ ἐφύβρισας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Andr.</u>
					624
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφύβριζον ἄλλα τε καὶ εἰ . .
			</span> they <i>gave vent to insulting language</i>, asking
			especially whether . . , <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.63
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>exult maliciously</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				955
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
